::MCQ::
What does a compiler do with source code?
{
~ Execute it line by line
= Convert it entirely into a binary/executable
~ Ignore optimization possibilities
~ Create platform-independent code
}

::MCQ::
Which characteristic best describes interpreted languages?
{
~ High execution speed
~ Platform-specific deployment
~ Complex bug detection
= Line-by-line compilation/execution
}

::MCQ::
What is a primary drawback of compiled languages?
{
~ Slow execution speed
~ Difficult debugging
= Need to compile for each target system
~ Limited optimization
}

::MCQ::
Both interpreted and compiled languages can create functional applications.
{
= True
~ False
}
